Off-by-one: the loop uses `i <= diff`, which removes `diff+1` entries. When `size >= Len()`, `diff` is clamped to 0 but the loop still runs once, evicting the oldest entry. Fix:Adding a test case for resize with capacity ≥ length:Fixed: off-by-one in `simplelru.LRU.Resize` (simplelru/lru.go:161). The eviction loop was `i <= diff`, so it always removed `diff+1` entries — even when `size >= Len()` (where `diff` clamps to 0), it still evicted the oldest entry. Changed to `i < diff`, added test cases, and all tests pass.